From 181d67f1fbdf92d439c140df0642fbb93507c190 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:40:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] serve an expired same-key clean WAL-holder verdict
 while one pass refreshes it

Under GIL load a macOS libproc holder pass outran its 5 s budget, so every
writable SessionDB open after each 30 s clean-verdict TTL blocked for 5 s
(49 'deleted-WAL holder scan timed out' lines in one hour on laptop-1,
2026-11-12, against Desktop deadlines of 4-10 s).

_iter_darwin_sidecar_holders now returns [] at once when the cached clean
verdict has expired but its key (sidecar identity incl. birth time) is
unchanged and the pass that produced it is younger than
_DARWIN_FD_STALE_CLEAN_MAX_SECONDS (300 s); it starts or joins the
single-flight pass without waiting, which publishes under the usual rules.
A holder now also voids any earlier clean verdict, so a positive is never
served stale. A changed key, no prior verdict, or one older than 300 s
keeps the blocking join and fail-open. Linux /proc walks synchronously on
the caller with no single-flight pass, so it is left alone.

